    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28662" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnĕcles</span></b> , is,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μενεκλῆς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an Asiatic rhetorician
				from Alabanda</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 23, 95</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Or. 69,
				231</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕ-nĕclĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Menecles the rhetorician</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Meneclium studium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 95, 326</span></i>
			.</div>
